<h2 class="bde-heading-1942-121 bde-heading">
Make the Numbers Make Sense</h2><p class="bde-f-text-1942-122 bde-f-text">
A salary figure is only the beginning. The useful questions are how a deal changes over time, what a team has committed to future seasons, and how those decisions affect the rest of its roster.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-1942-123 bde-f-text">
NBA Salaries brings those details together in player profiles, team pages and clear visual comparisons. Our aim is to make a complicated part of basketball easier to explore.
</p>
</div><div id="coverage" class="bde-fancy-container-1942-107 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-1942-124 bde-heading">
Follow the Player. Understand the Team</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-1942-125 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-1942-135 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-1942-143 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-1942-158 bde-f-text">
Players
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-1942-144 bde-heading">
A Contract in Context
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-1942-145 bde-f-text">
Annual salaries, contract periods, options and career earnings, with estimated net worth clearly labeled.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-1942-136 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-1942-146 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-1942-159 bde-f-text">
Teams
</div>
